WEBVTT

00:00:02.610 --> 00:00:05.590
Present Day

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:08.540
Present Time

00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:23.290
And you don't seem to understand

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:28.490
A shame you seemed an honest man

00:00:26.740 --> 00:00:33.240
And all the fears you hold so dear

00:00:31.870 --> 00:00:38.510
Will turn to whisper in your ear

00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:41.910
And you know what they say might hurt you

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:44.380
And you know that it means so much

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:49.140
And you don't even feel a thing

00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:54.800
I am falling, I am fading

00:00:52.990 --> 00:00:58.920
I have lost it all

00:01:17.670 --> 00:01:26.940
I am falling, I am fading, I am drowning

00:01:25.390 --> 00:01:29.580
Help me to breathe

00:01:27.610 --> 00:01:34.790
I am hurting, I have lost it all

00:01:33.150 --> 00:01:37.330
I am losing

00:01:35.720 --> 00:01:41.530
Help me to breathe

00:02:38.440 --> 00:02:42.010
There is only one truth. God.

00:02:51.420 --> 00:02:53.760
Yes. Me.

00:02:55.320 --> 00:02:57.670
Isn't that right, Lain?

00:03:17.710 --> 00:03:20.450
You're God?

00:03:21.580 --> 00:03:24.920
Yes. I am God.

00:03:32.390 --> 00:03:37.040
Why are you God? I don't understand.

00:03:41.700 --> 00:03:45.380
You're dead, aren't you? A dead human.

00:03:45.380 --> 00:03:49.150
Somebody like that can't be God, can they?

00:03:52.140 --> 00:03:55.570
I realized that I had no need for a body.

00:03:56.650 --> 00:04:00.540
To die is merely to abandon the flesh.

00:04:03.550 --> 00:04:06.420
That's... That's just what Chisa said.

00:04:09.980 --> 00:04:12.480
I don't need to stay here.

00:04:14.260 --> 00:04:16.940
I suppose she did, at that.

00:04:18.600 --> 00:04:21.930
I caused the protocol that governs the Wired to evolve.

00:04:23.740 --> 00:04:26.560
Yeah. That's what you did.

00:04:27.040 --> 00:04:29.940
But a protocol is just an agreement.

00:04:29.940 --> 00:04:37.200
Yes, but I incorporated code that operates on a higher phase.

00:04:38.120 --> 00:04:39.240
So?

00:04:43.330 --> 00:04:48.250
There is compressed information mixed into the protocol.

00:04:49.570 --> 00:04:51.170
What kind of information?

00:04:51.170 --> 00:04:54.260
Human memories. Mine.

00:04:54.520 --> 00:04:59.720
The thoughts, history, memories, and emotions of the man named Eiri Masami.

00:05:01.610 --> 00:05:04.760
What does that mean?

00:05:06.180 --> 00:05:10.510
I can live forever as an anonymous entity in the Wired,

00:05:10.510 --> 00:05:13.570
and will be able to rule it with information.

00:05:14.990 --> 00:05:18.110
What do you think a being like that should be called?

00:05:19.430 --> 00:05:20.660
A god.

00:05:20.950 --> 00:05:22.820
There is no God.

00:05:25.500 --> 00:05:30.150
Yes. Even if I were an omnipresent being and could influence others,

00:05:30.540 --> 00:05:33.380
with no one to worship me, I am no god.

00:05:34.340 --> 00:05:38.590
But you had them. Or made them, I should say.

00:05:40.480 --> 00:05:42.180
Knights.

00:05:58.200 --> 00:06:02.950
You no longer need a body, Lain.

00:06:06.780 --> 00:06:08.790
That's a lie!

00:06:16.970 --> 00:06:18.800
Talk about lame!

00:06:27.730 --> 00:06:29.850
Some people are like that, I guess.

00:06:30.120 --> 00:06:32.450
So I said, go ahead and do it.

00:06:32.450 --> 00:06:33.790
Anyway...

00:06:33.790 --> 00:06:35.650
Hey, look at this!

00:06:35.650 --> 00:06:37.790
Isn't it cute?

00:06:39.530 --> 00:06:42.130
It was really cheap!

00:06:42.130 --> 00:06:42.930
At that place next door?

00:06:42.930 --> 00:06:43.860
Yeah, over there!

00:06:45.050 --> 00:06:45.860
Let's go, let's go!

00:06:46.950 --> 00:06:48.810
Sure, we don't have anything after school today.

00:06:48.810 --> 00:06:50.250
Hey, you're right.

00:06:50.250 --> 00:06:51.300
Let's go!

00:07:05.500 --> 00:07:06.850
Stand!

00:07:09.140 --> 00:07:10.780
Bow!

00:07:13.440 --> 00:07:15.860
All right, close your books.

00:07:42.570 --> 00:07:46.650
I... I'm real!

00:07:46.650 --> 00:07:48.770
I'm alive!

00:07:48.770 --> 00:07:51.100
I'm here.

00:07:52.080 --> 00:07:54.810
Why is this happening?

00:07:55.550 --> 00:07:58.180
Was it something I did?

00:07:58.180 --> 00:08:03.010
I always tried to keep something like this from happening.

00:08:03.010 --> 00:08:06.950
I always tried not to say anything weird.

00:08:08.030 --> 00:08:10.550
Can it be true?

00:08:11.700 --> 00:08:14.920
I'm not supposed to have a body?

00:08:18.910 --> 00:08:20.500
That's right, Lain.

00:08:21.850 --> 00:08:25.010
You're not needed in the real world.

00:09:24.370 --> 00:09:25.570
I'm home.

00:10:49.830 --> 00:10:51.240
Dad?

00:10:51.900 --> 00:10:55.370
This is goodbye, Miss Lain.

00:10:57.830 --> 00:11:02.910
You must have figured it out by now. Our work here is finished.

00:11:03.970 --> 00:11:07.800
It was only for a short time, but I know I didn't do enough for you.

00:11:07.800 --> 00:11:11.160
You're now free to become anything you want.

00:11:11.950 --> 00:11:14.640
No, you were free all along.

00:11:15.590 --> 00:11:21.640
I wasn't given permission to say goodbye, but I loved you.

00:11:26.230 --> 00:11:29.580
It's not that I enjoyed playing house...

00:11:30.070 --> 00:11:35.180
Maybe I envied a being like you.

00:11:35.840 --> 00:11:37.360
Goodbye.

00:11:45.050 --> 00:11:45.960
Wait!

00:11:47.920 --> 00:11:49.970
Don't leave me alone!

00:11:51.590 --> 00:11:55.800
Alone? You're not alone.

00:11:58.260 --> 00:12:02.980
If you connect to the Wired, everyone will welcome you.

00:12:02.980 --> 00:12:06.450
That's the sort of being you were.

00:12:27.260 --> 00:12:29.290
I'm not alone.

00:12:41.610 --> 00:12:44.060
Do you want to do anything, Lain?

00:12:48.380 --> 00:12:50.970
This is your world, Lain.

00:12:53.150 --> 00:12:58.210
Who are the Knights? They're the ones who made the fake me, right?

00:12:58.590 --> 00:13:00.110
I'm not sure.

00:13:00.110 --> 00:13:01.280
No, it's possible.

00:13:01.790 --> 00:13:04.050
They say you can trace the origin of the

00:13:04.050 --> 00:13:07.240
Knights of the Eastern Calculus back to the Knights Templar.

00:13:07.600 --> 00:13:12.060
They've used that invisible human network, the collective unconscious,

00:13:12.060 --> 00:13:16.300
since long before the Wired was born.

00:13:18.010 --> 00:13:20.360
What do you want to do, Lain?

00:13:21.580 --> 00:13:23.030
Knights...

00:13:23.030 --> 00:13:25.030
Who are the Knights?

00:13:25.950 --> 00:13:28.270
You really want to know, don't you, Lain?

00:13:29.520 --> 00:13:34.830
The Wired's God is a god because He has worshipers.

00:14:02.090 --> 00:14:05.440
Hey, Taro, let's go someplace else.

00:14:05.960 --> 00:14:07.840
This place has gotten boring.

00:14:07.840 --> 00:14:10.710
Yeah. Why not come over to my house?

00:14:10.710 --> 00:14:13.050
You don't need to come, Masayuki.

00:14:14.860 --> 00:14:16.470
What's the big idea?

00:14:17.070 --> 00:14:21.020
Taro says he doesn't wanna hang out with a little kid like you.

00:14:21.370 --> 00:14:22.780
Wha...?

00:14:22.780 --> 00:14:25.220
You're as much a kid as I am, Myu-Myu!

00:14:26.910 --> 00:14:31.290
It's okay for a girl! Everybody knows that younger is better for girls.

00:14:31.580 --> 00:14:32.930
Right, Taro?

00:14:33.280 --> 00:14:34.700
What's that?

00:14:34.700 --> 00:14:38.970
What's up, Taro? Is there something on the Net News?

00:14:39.660 --> 00:14:40.880
It's a list.

00:14:40.880 --> 00:14:42.800
Huh? What kind of list?

00:14:43.490 --> 00:14:48.270
What's a list of Knights members doing on the Net News?

00:15:04.110 --> 00:15:05.570
Y-Yes?

00:15:11.290 --> 00:15:13.080
Please remain silent.

00:15:14.860 --> 00:15:16.090
W-Who are you?

00:15:16.450 --> 00:15:18.150
Time to pay the piper, all right?

00:15:18.150 --> 00:15:19.480
W-What do you mean?

00:15:52.530 --> 00:15:54.670
Mom, I got killed!

00:15:54.670 --> 00:15:56.380
Mom!

00:15:57.200 --> 00:16:01.090
It's your turn, Mom! If you don't hurry up, I'm gonna keep playing!

00:16:01.640 --> 00:16:03.630
Okay, Mom?

00:16:04.770 --> 00:16:07.660
I'm gonna take 'em out!

00:16:11.210 --> 00:16:15.240
A series of suicides occurred today all over the world,

00:16:15.240 --> 00:16:18.010
and each country's Information Control Ministry

00:16:18.010 --> 00:16:20.070
and police departments have begun investigating the cause.

00:16:20.790 --> 00:16:25.350
Each victim was involved in network-related work,

00:16:25.350 --> 00:16:29.070
and sources tell us that it appears that they were all members

00:16:29.070 --> 00:16:32.320
of a fraternal order known as the "Knights."

00:17:18.450 --> 00:17:22.090
Why did you do it?

00:17:23.050 --> 00:17:26.200
It was a request from our client.

00:17:26.890 --> 00:17:31.070
You hunted down all the Knights in the world.

00:17:31.070 --> 00:17:35.310
Our associates are now on their way to dispose of them.

00:17:36.030 --> 00:17:38.230
But why?

00:17:38.940 --> 00:17:42.180
The Wired can't be allowed to be a special world.

00:17:42.840 --> 00:17:47.780
It can only be a field that functions as a sub-system reinforcing the real world.

00:17:49.110 --> 00:17:51.030
But still...

00:17:51.510 --> 00:17:56.240
You can't be allowed to exist in the Wired, either.

00:17:56.240 --> 00:17:58.370
But here you are, safe and sound.

00:18:00.260 --> 00:18:04.440
Some god or whatever must be protecting you.

00:18:06.930 --> 00:18:10.450
Eiri Masami's residual thought program

00:18:10.450 --> 00:18:13.180
will eventually be disinfected from the Wired.

00:18:13.180 --> 00:18:20.810
Our client is working on a total rewrite of the Protocol Seven code.

00:18:24.110 --> 00:18:27.110
We have no need for gods.

00:18:27.110 --> 00:18:30.730
Right. Not in the Wired or in the real world.

00:18:46.000 --> 00:18:51.090
We still haven't figured out what you are.

00:18:56.550 --> 00:18:59.890
But I love you.

00:19:03.390 --> 00:19:08.390
Love certainly is a strange emotion, isn't it?

00:19:36.050 --> 00:19:37.640
What will you do?

00:19:38.620 --> 00:19:41.840
Well, let me think...

00:19:44.860 --> 00:19:47.750
You don't have anyone to pray to you now.

00:19:50.100 --> 00:19:55.210
I can't be a god, then. But I haven't lost all of them.

00:19:55.610 --> 00:20:00.080
If only one believer remains, I can still be a god.

00:20:00.980 --> 00:20:02.290
Who?

00:20:03.280 --> 00:20:06.750
Come, now... You, Lain.

00:20:10.290 --> 00:20:14.380
It's because of me that you can stay yourself.

00:20:14.820 --> 00:20:18.810
You were originally born in the Wired.

00:20:18.810 --> 00:20:24.260
The legend of the Wired. The heroine of the Wired's fairy tales.

00:20:30.140 --> 00:20:31.590
Liar.

00:20:32.540 --> 00:20:36.830
The real world's Iwakura Lain is merely a hologram of her.

00:20:36.830 --> 00:20:39.950
A homunculus of artificial ribosomes.

00:20:40.720 --> 00:20:43.530
You never had a body to begin with.

00:20:44.950 --> 00:20:46.540
That's a lie.

00:20:47.890 --> 00:20:53.760
A fake family. Fake friends. Yes, it was all a lie.

00:20:56.330 --> 00:20:57.850
That's a lie...

00:21:00.170 --> 00:21:02.260
That's all a lie...

00:21:04.680 --> 00:21:08.690
Poor Lain... She's all alone.

00:21:09.010 --> 00:21:13.360
But I'm here. The man who loves you is here.

00:21:13.880 --> 00:21:18.500
You should be able to love me, the man who sent you to this world...

00:21:20.820 --> 00:21:24.330
I am your creator.

00:21:24.890 --> 00:21:27.330
Love me.

00:21:28.330 --> 00:21:30.680
All right, Lain?

00:21:31.500 --> 00:21:33.340
The other...

00:21:35.740 --> 00:21:37.830
The other me, she's...

00:21:37.830 --> 00:21:42.760
That isn't another you. It's the real you.

00:21:46.550 --> 00:21:48.760
Like it matters!

00:22:29.100 --> 00:22:33.530
nan no tsumi mo nai hazu na no ni

00:22:29.100 --> 00:22:33.530
Although I must be innocent,

00:22:33.530 --> 00:22:37.440
nanraka no batsu wo uketeru

00:22:33.530 --> 00:22:37.440
now I am punished.

00:22:37.870 --> 00:22:43.740
jibun de maita tane de mo nai no ni

00:22:37.870 --> 00:22:43.740
I wasn't the one who sowed those seeds, but nevertheless

00:22:44.460 --> 00:22:50.650
sakimidareta hana tsumasareru

00:22:44.460 --> 00:22:50.650
I have to pull up the flowers that bloomed from them.

00:22:57.200 --> 00:23:01.840
shiranai koto to mo ienai ga

00:22:57.200 --> 00:23:01.840
I can't say I didn't know about it,

00:23:01.840 --> 00:23:06.290
katabou katsuida oboe wa nai

00:23:01.840 --> 00:23:06.290
but I don't remember taking any part in it.

00:23:06.290 --> 00:23:12.480
jiyuu wo takaku kawasareta ki mo suru ga

00:23:06.290 --> 00:23:12.480
I think my freedom cost me dearly,

00:23:13.010 --> 00:23:19.720
kokoro made yasuku utta oboe wa nai

00:23:13.010 --> 00:23:19.720
but I don't remember selling my soul so cheaply.

00:23:20.080 --> 00:23:27.770
Hey Hey kutabatte osaraba suru made

00:23:20.080 --> 00:23:27.770
Hey hey, until I die and say farewell...

00:23:28.790 --> 00:23:37.680
Hey Hey dare no te ni mo kakaranai

00:23:28.790 --> 00:23:37.680
Hey hey... no one can touch me.

00:23:39.200 --> 00:23:43.290
tooi yoru wo urotsuiteiru

00:23:39.200 --> 00:23:43.290
You probably don't know

00:23:43.290 --> 00:23:51.000
shiranai darou eien no narazu monotachi wo

00:23:43.290 --> 00:23:51.000
the eternal outlaws prowling in the distant night.
